### Mutations that did not turn red (not used)
- The loaders keep the first record of each snapshot version (the plan's
  example): not tried as a guard. The switch removes the older segments
  right after its rename, so a normal run leaves one record per version.
- The engine keeps a manifest list (`Blob::ManifestList`) of the target tag
  as is: no test turned red. A manifest list is written when the content of
  its file is set (`set_manifest`), under the same hash as that content key,
  and an unchanged file keeps its list. So a target-tag manifest list over
  keys of another tag does not come up on these stores. The D-14 case is a file root (a value) of the
  target tag over old chunks, which mutation B2 covers.

## Task 2: crash_* and verify_*

Command: cargo test -p slicefs-cli --test rehash_tests -- crash verify

### Run 1: mutations G1, G2 and G3
- G1 (rehash.rs): no `cs.sync()` before the switch.
- G2 (rehash.rs and segment/switch.rs): no `remove_switch_tmps`.
- G3 (rehash.rs): on an engine error, write a switch segment (old roots)
  before the error is returned.

